    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/alpine/line-chart/v2`** (gate 8; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Props = showcase defaults (Monthly Active Users). v1 deprecated → rides base·dep.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | not internal, not deprecated | confirm |\n| Gate | — | **base** |\n| Preview assets | re-mint after approval | review |\n| Cover / Tutorial | neither | needed? (left→right draw-on starts near-blank → cover likely) |\n\n**Pre-audit: CLEANEST YET — zero code changes.** The flagged insetNode callsites (tick rail + category labels) verified safe empirically: feasibility green ×14 canvases ×6 configs (incl. grid-8, linear curve, area/points off, dark). Visuals clean at landscape/portrait/ultrawide/prime-small — labels decimate correctly at narrow widths (Jan/Mar/May/Jul), ticks align.\n\n**No debugLayout contract on this one, deliberately:** the plot (line, area, markers, grid) is mask-unified — all point markers live in ONE combined mask source, so there is no repeated labeled geometry to express a contract over. A hollow contract would be noise.\n\n**Axis note (design, not a bug):** month labels sit BETWEEN points — 9 data points = interval boundaries, 8 labels = the spans. Consistent at every canvas.\n\n**Stress:** mints after your default verdict.",
