        "text": "YOUR AXIS RULING IS IN — and your eye was right twice over:\n\n1. **The \"interval labels\" were never a design** — it was an edge-clamp bug: label cells were a full spacing wide, and the FIRST label's cell clamped at the plot edge, pushing \"Jan\" ~half a spacing right of its point. Cells now SHRINK near the edges so every label centers ON its point (it was always 8 labels ↔ 8 points).\n2. **X-axis ticks added** — a small real rect under each labeled point (ticks follow the decimated labels, so tile count stays flat at high N).\n3. **The contract extension you proposed** landed in the PRIMITIVE: `xCenters`/`yCenters` (absolute px) and `xCentersFrac`/`yCentersFrac` (group-relative span fractions — model-free, immune to origin-chain drift). The template uses the frac lock: every tick must sit at its point's span-fraction. Two build lessons en route: tick weights are authored AT the serializer's 120 basis so emitted = intended; and tolerance is 0.06 (not 0.02) because the frames↔sources zip noise from the kpi candidate also touches this doc when points/area are off — the class this guards (a tick a full spacing off) is ≥0.14, still 2.3× the tolerance.\n\nLOOK-SHIFT: ticks are new chrome + Jan/Aug now center on their dots. 43/43 unit (incl. 7-canvas tick-lock + no-labels-no-ticks), contract suite 75/75, battery ×14 canvases ×6 configs, e2e 4/4. Cover already in from your earlier ruling."
